<title>UK: NW Europe offshore oil, gas rigs steady in week.</title>
<headline>NW Europe offshore oil, gas rigs steady in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation offshore northwest Europe stood unchanged at 58 in the week to December 11, consultants Arthur Andersen said in a report.</p>
<p>Year-on-year, combined exploration spuds in the U.K., Norway and the Netherlands were up 18 percent, Andersen said.</p>
<p>U.K. rigs fell one to 29 while Norwegian activity rose by one rig to 17. There were eight rigs active in Dutch waters, flat from a week earlier as was Denmark with four rigs.</p>
<p>Onshore U.K. drilling was steady at three rigs.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
